# Git cadence — commit very often (mandatory for ALL agents)

1. **Commit very frequently.** Commit after every passing test, every finished
   sub-step, and at least every 30 minutes of work. Small commits, Conventional
   Commit messages. Never hold more than ~30 minutes of uncommitted work.
2. **Push after every commit** to your own `feat/<owner>/<scope>` branch, so
   teammates and their agents can see your work. An unpushed commit is
   invisible to everyone else.
3. **Always read what changed before you act.** At session start, before every
   commit and push, before changing any shared interface, and before opening or
   updating a PR, run `git fetch origin --prune` and review
   `git log --oneline HEAD..origin/main` plus `git diff --stat HEAD...origin/main`.
4. **Integrate often.** Merge or rebase `origin/main` into your branch at least
   daily and whenever main changes something you depend on (commit or stash
   first; never force-push shared branches).
5. Human-only git attribution applies (see `human-only-git-attribution.mdc`):
   never an agent identity, never attribution trailers.
